      ":question/id": "7d7f9633-00ce-5100-9a7b-a0c897990417",
      ":question/problem": "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary row operations of the form $R_{i}:=R_{i}+kR_{2},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary row operations?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make the entries above and below $a_{21}=1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n\\xrightarrow{R_{1}:=R_{1}-R_{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n\\xrightarrow{R_{3}:=R_{3}-2R_{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}=B\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$R_{1}:=R_{1}-R_{2}$ and $R_{3}:=R_{3}-2R_{2}$.",
